{"id":7355446939269,"type":"album","name":"The Ape of Naples","artist":"Coil","year":2005,"weight":12,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/29436-the-ape-of-naples_174502.jpg","aoty":90,"aoty_user":83,"yt":"INMo0sj9AMw","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/coil/the-ape-of-naples/","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/29436-coil-the-ape-of-naples.php"},"desc":"As the last album recorded during John Balance's lifetime, The Ape of Naples serves as a final statement and summation of the band's multi-faceted career. The album is more of a \"classic\"-sounding Coil album (in the vein of Love's Secret Domain and Musick to Play in the Dark, Vol. 1) than more recent outings (such as ANS, Constant Shallowness Leads to Evil, or Astral Disaster). Ape is made up of recording sessions that date back to the mid-'90s, recordings done for Trent Reznor's nothing label, and more recent works that were still getting worked out in a live environment (\"Triple ."},"artist_ref":{"id":233770364598869,"name":"Coil","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Coil_band_Portraited.png?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":15318882910861,"type":"genre","name":"Post-Industrial","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":224,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":208607141602166,"name":"RYM Top — Industrial & Noise — Post-Industrial","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":8,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":219177945805128,"name":"RYM Top — Industrial & Noise","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":8,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":150848509715573,"name":"RYM Top — Experimental","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":9,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":72396664188223,"name":"Sputnikmusic Best Albums 2005","src":"charts","grp":"sputnikmusic","list_year":null,"rank":25,"year